#doc(title: [Pendulum practical: results], subject: "Year 12 physics")

= The simple pendulum

The period $T$ of a simple pendulum of length $l$ is $T = 2 pi sqrt(l / g)$ for small swings. Each student timed ten oscillations for each length, and the table gives the period found.#footnote[Timing ten oscillations divides the reaction-time error by ten.] A graph of $T^2$ against $l$ is a straight line through the origin, whose gradient is $4 pi^2 / g$.

